> f(x: u4, y: u4, z: u4, t: u4) = y*t*z + x*t
> g(x: u4, y: u4, z: u4, t: u4) = (y*z + x)*t
> f2(x: u4, y: u4, z: u4, t: u4) = (y*t*z + x*t) + 0
> g2(x: u4, y: u4, z: u4, t: u4) = ((y*z + x)*t) + 0
> f1(x: u4, y: u4, z: u4, t: u4) = (y*t*z + x*t) + 0
> equiv f g
f and g are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
> equiv f2 g2
f2 and g2 are equal on the domain of f2 (exhaustive)
> equiv f1 g
f1 and g are equal on the domain of f1 (exhaustive)
> equiv f f2
f and f2 are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
